  "$e2e": 1,
  "id": "brief.agency-site",
  "title": "ULTRA milestone — agency site from brief (pages + theme builder + design system + popups + rollback + cross-doc compensation)",
  "_comment": "WP-Q07 declarative brief. This is NOT the LOCKED §2 envelope (kind/expect etc.) — it is a custom e2e brief shape ($e2e:1) read DIRECTLY by packages/server/src/test-harness/e2e-scenario.ts, NOT by the generic fixture-loader (fixtures/e2e/** is not in FIXTURE_SUBDIRS, so fixtures:validate skips it). It drives the M1-M8 end-to-end run (00-product-overview.md §6) over the live MCP/REST surface: create pages + build the styled-primed hero (M1), apply a design system via the diff-PUT (M5) + watermarked variables batch, stand up a Pro header/footer + popup (M6, gated behind Pro), make a safe edit then rollback (M2), and run a cross-doc batch.apply with a FORCED partial failure to exercise best-effort compensation + E_COMPENSATION_FAILED (M8). Every authoring node uses TYPED prop envelopes ([R8] — the live 4.1.1 validator rejects bare strings). Pro conditions are ConditionTuple [type,name,sub_name?,sub_id?] arrays — the companion writes them via Conditions_Manager::save_conditions() which slash-joins + regenerates cache (SUPPLEMENT §A.1); the brief never writes _elementor_conditions raw. Expected end-state assertions live in expected.outcomes.json.",

