  "batch": {
    "_comment": "M8 cross-doc transaction (10-rest-api.md §13). batch.apply records backups of the kit + every touched doc UP FRONT, executes steps in order, and on a partial failure best-effort compensates (reverse-order restore) + returns a per-step result map {step_index,ok,output,error,compensated}. A failed step is NOT an HTTP error — the per-step results[] carries it; HTTP is 200 unless the request is malformed (400) or compensation itself failed (500 E_COMPENSATION_FAILED). The plan below has a deliberately INVALID step 2 (a save with a bare-string prop the validator rejects → E_ATOMIC_VALIDATION) AFTER a valid step 1, forcing the partial failure + compensation of step 1.",
    "plan": [
      {
        "ref": "batch-page-ok",
        "route": "documents/save",
        "title": "Q07 Batch OK page",
        "expect_ok": true,
        "tree": [
